<div class="section-head">
<div class="section-num">GENERAL PLAN UPDATE</div>
<h2 class="section-title">Santa Fe Forward: step 4 of 5, no adoption date set</h2>
<p class="section-note">Per the project's own five-step framing at santafeforward.org.</p>
</div>

<div class="steps">
<div class="step done"><span class="step-marker"></span><div class="step-body"><div class="step-top"><h3>1. Project Launch</h3><span class="step-state">Complete</span></div><p>First open house, public engagement kicked off, Draft Assessment Report published for public review.</p></div></div>
<div class="step done"><span class="step-marker"></span><div class="step-body"><div class="step-top"><h3>2. Vision and Goals</h3><span class="step-state">Complete</span></div><p>Community input shaped the priorities behind the Vision Summary's mission and eight topic-area goals.</p></div></div>
<div class="step done"><span class="step-marker"></span><div class="step-body"><div class="step-top"><h3>3. Scenario Planning</h3><span class="step-state">Complete</span></div><p>The project team refined land-use scenarios based on community feedback and technical analysis.</p></div></div>
<div class="step active"><span class="step-marker"></span><div class="step-body"><div class="step-top"><h3>4. Updated General Plan</h3><span class="step-state">Active now</span></div><p>Emerging recommendations and a thematic planning map are under review. The site flags a public open house for November 7, 2026 covering this material.</p></div></div>
<div class="step upcoming"><span class="step-marker"></span><div class="step-body"><div class="step-top"><h3>5. Moving Forward</h3><span class="step-state">Not started</span></div><p>Governing Body action, implementation, and evaluation. No target date for a draft plan document or adoption has been published — the city's own FAQ says engagement continues "over the next few years."</p></div></div>
</div>

<div class="case-study-list" style="margin-top:22px;">

<article class="card case-study" id="gp-assessment">
<div class="card-top">
<h3>Assessment Report — key findings, condensed</h3>
<span class="cs-tag">18 chapters · published</span>
</div>
<span class="field-label">What it found</span>
<p>Roughly a third of Santa Fe households are cost-burdened — 39% of owners and 49% of renters spend more than 30% of income on housing. Housing is 67% single-unit (detached or attached), and 68% of zoned parcels are residential, which the report ties directly to both the affordability and walkability gaps this update is meant to address. An estimated 5,500 vacant acres are developable, with another 1,000 acres underused. The city's own equity analysis flags 13 census tracts — concentrated west of St. Francis Drive — carrying the highest combined household, transportation, and environmental burden. On the 1999 General Plan's record: more than half its policies were only partially implemented or remain ongoing after 25 years, and several — a defined neighborhood-center designation, an infill zoning classification, most downtown parking reforms — were never implemented at all.</p>
<span class="field-label">Sources</span>
<div class="src-row"><a href="/pdf-library/#pdf-assessment">PDF Library — full 18-chapter set ↓</a>
<a href="https://santafeforward.org/learn-more#report" target="_blank" rel="noopener">santafeforward.org — Assessment Report ↗</a></div>
</article>

<article class="card case-study" id="gp-vision">
<div class="card-top">
<h3>Vision Summary</h3>
<span class="cs-tag">July 2026 · published</span>
</div>
<span class="field-label">What it says</span>
<p>A mission statement and eight topic-area goals (People &amp; Housing, History/Culture/Arts, Engagement &amp; Governance, Education/Social/Economic Opportunity, Nature/Sustainability/Resiliency, Community Services &amp; Utilities, Transportation, The Built City), each paired with a short "What We'll Do" commitment. The language is goal-level — it names priorities, not specific policies, standards, or numbers. Translating it into actionable language is what the current "Updated General Plan" step, and the eventual draft plan, are meant to do.</p>
<span class="field-label">Sources</span>
<div class="src-row"><a href="/pdf-library/#pdf-assessment">PDF Library — Vision Summary ↓</a>
<a href="https://santafeforward.org/get-involved/vision-summary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">santafeforward.org — Vision Summary ↗</a></div>
<p class="muted" style="margin-top:10px;">See <a href="/recommendations/#rec-guide">General Plan Language Comparisons</a> for how this reads against other adopted plans' vision language.</p>
</article>

