<section class="sub" id="status-drm">
<div class="section-head">
<div class="section-num">DEVELOPMENT REVIEW</div>
<h2 class="section-title">No standalone manual exists — here's what the process actually is</h2>
<p class="section-note">The Current Planning page doesn't publish a single "Development Review Manual." What it publishes instead, translated into plain language:</p>
</div>

<div class="card-grid">
<article class="card">
<div class="card-top"><h3>1. Pre-Application</h3></div>
<p>An applicant meets with planning staff before filing, to identify which review type and application form(s) apply and flag issues early.</p>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="card-top"><h3>2. Development Review</h3></div>
<p>Staff review against the applicable standards. Most individual application types (rezoning, master plan, development plan, and others) each have their own numbered form in the PLUD series.</p>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="card-top"><h3>3. Public Hearing</h3></div>
<p>Where required, the application goes to a public body (Planning Commission, Governing Body, or similar) on a published hearing calendar.</p>
</article>
</div>

